WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.780
If the pictures are too good and
don't live up to their promise,

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.700
that damages the restaurant guest's trust.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.420
And if they're too poor, we
simply lose our appetite.

4
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.100
Why do people react negatively
to AI-generated images of food?

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.780
Through evolution we
have learned to be very

6
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.780
alert to when something is
slightly wrong with food.

7
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:29.100
It's something that signals to us
that it isn't good for us to eat.

8
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.040
Food has also been used a great deal
in advertising, because we know

9
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
that pictures of appetizing food make us
hungry, so it affects us physiologically.

10
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.700
And precisely this, that food
images affect us physiologically,

11
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.960
is what I think gives us such
a strong reaction to it.

12
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.320
Will our attitude towards
AI images change over time?

13
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.460
I believe so.

14
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.620
There is a concept in psychology
research called technology acceptance.

15
00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.560
How accepting we are of new technology.

16
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.820
And it means that the more
knowledge we gain about something,

17
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.460
the more we use it and the more

18
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.260
we see it around us in our everyday lives,

19
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.880
the more accepting we become
of this new technology.

